---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
import { generateBreadcrumbSchema } from '../../utils/seo';

const title = 'Costs & Ownership Reference';
const description = 'Home Reference integrates replacement costs and lifecycle economics directly into individual equipment manuals rather than maintaining separate speculative pricing estimates.';
const schema = generateBreadcrumbSchema([
  { name: 'Home', item: '/' },
  { name: 'Costs & Ownership', item: '/costs/' },
]);
---

<BaseLayout
  title={title}
  description={description}
  canonicalUrl="https://homereference.org/costs/"
  currentPath="/costs/"
  schemaJson={schema}
  noindex={true}
>
  <div class="py-12 max-w-3xl mx-auto space-y-8">
    <div class="border-b border-[#E5DFD7] pb-6">
      <span class="text-xs font-mono uppercase tracking-widest text-[#78716C] block mb-2">
        Editorial Organization Note
      </span>
      <h1 class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl font-serif font-bold text-[#1C1917] tracking-tight">
        Equipment Costs & Ownership Economics
      </h1>
    </div>

    <div class="prose text-[#57534E] space-y-4 text-sm sm:text-base leading-relaxed font-serif">
      <p>
        At Home Reference, we intentionally avoid publishing flat, generic national cost averages. Trade labor rates, local municipal permit requirements, regional climate sizing, and equipment efficiency mandates cause real-world installation quotes to vary by 50% to 100% between markets.
      </p>
      <p>
        Instead of maintaining an isolated, speculative pricing catalog, <strong>capital replacement factors, repair-versus-replace guidelines, and efficiency cost trade-offs are directly integrated into each individual equipment guide:</strong>
      </p>
    </div>

    <div class="grid grid-cols-1 sm:grid-cols-2 gap-4 pt-2">
      <a
        href="/systems/water-heater-lifespan-and-replacement/"
        class="p-5 bg-white border border-[#E5DFD7] hover:border-[#8C4736] transition-colors rounded-none group"
      >
        <span class="text-xs font-mono text-[#8C4736] block mb-1">Water Heating</span>
        <h2 class="font-serif font-bold text-base text-[#1C1917] group-hover:text-[#8C4736] transition-colors">
          Water Heater Replacement & Economics →
        </h2>
        <p class="text-xs text-[#78716C] mt-2">
          Anode replacement ROI, tank vs. tankless capital factors, and sediment failure indicators.
        </p>
      </a>

      <a
        href="/systems/central-ac-lifespan-and-efficiency/"
        class="p-5 bg-white border border-[#E5DFD7] hover:border-[#8C4736] transition-colors rounded-none group"
      >
        <span class="text-xs font-mono text-[#8C4736] block mb-1">HVAC Cooling</span>
        <h2 class="font-serif font-bold text-base text-[#1C1917] group-hover:text-[#8C4736] transition-colors">
          Central A/C Lifespan & SEER2 Efficiency →
        </h2>
        <p class="text-xs text-[#78716C] mt-2">
          Compressor failure economics, refrigerant phase-outs, and ductwork compatibility.
        </p>
      </a>

      <a
        href="/systems/furnace-lifespan-and-replacement/"
        class="p-5 bg-white border border-[#E5DFD7] hover:border-[#8C4736] transition-colors rounded-none group"
      >
        <span class="text-xs font-mono text-[#8C4736] block mb-1">Heating</span>
        <h2 class="font-serif font-bold text-base text-[#1C1917] group-hover:text-[#8C4736] transition-colors">
          Furnace Replacement & Heat Exchanger Safety →
        </h2>
        <p class="text-xs text-[#78716C] mt-2">
          Evaluating 80% vs. 90%+ AFUE economics and secondary heat exchanger failure risks.
        </p>
      </a>

      <a
        href="/appliances/refrigerator-lifespan-and-maintenance/"
        class="p-5 bg-white border border-[#E5DFD7] hover:border-[#8C4736] transition-colors rounded-none group"
      >
        <span class="text-xs font-mono text-[#8C4736] block mb-1">Kitchen Appliances</span>
        <h2 class="font-serif font-bold text-base text-[#1C1917] group-hover:text-[#8C4736] transition-colors">
          Refrigerator Lifespan & Repair Thresholds →
        </h2>
        <p class="text-xs text-[#78716C] mt-2">
          The 50% repair rule of thumb, sealed system failure costs, and EPA Section 608 boundaries.
        </p>
      </a>
    </div>

    <div class="p-6 bg-[#F4EFEA] border border-[#E5DFD7] text-xs text-[#78716C] leading-relaxed">
      <strong>Indexing Notice:</strong> This section is marked with <code>noindex, follow</code> while standalone regional cost-index models are being evaluated for verifiable primary data. All links above point to fully verified, canonical reference guides.
    </div>
  </div>
</BaseLayout>
